[rexglue-native] SDK 0309, released in setup tool 2.31.0 (2026-11-04). Native depth resolves and resolve
records at a draw resolution scale (Vulkan; on top of 0308; only with native_resolves_at_draw_scale on).
Off, nothing changes.

With native_resolves_at_draw_scale on, depth resolves (and color whose red/blue order the texture can't
take) are done natively at the scale too: the pass writes the texture's texels at the scale into the
scratch buffer, converted as the scaled depth load shaders do (k_24_8, k_24_8_FLOAT, k_8_8_8_8), then a
buffer-to-image copy (scratch capped at 128 MB; past that it loads as before). A resolve with no scaled
texture yet is done natively as well, writing the scaled resolve buffer so the texture made later loads
right. New setting native_resolve_records_at_draw_scale (GPU, default off): each native color resolve is
recorded with the render target area it came from, and a scaled 8888 texture loaded later over that memory
is copied from the render target if nothing has drawn into or cleared it since; otherwise it loads from the
buffer as before.

Tested with 0308 (dev/agents/rexglue-native/R3-SCALE-ASYNC.md, R4-SCALE-TIMING.md,
R5-RELEASE-CANDIDATE.md): depth and records at 2x and 3x, 0 errors, pictures within noise.

